{
  "schema": "vault-prefs",
  "protocol_version": "v0.1",
  "spec_section": "protocol.md §9.5",
  "description": "Pins the protocol::encode_prefs_blob_raw + protocol::decode_prefs_blob byte mapping for cross-implementation conformance. vault.prefs is the v0.1 vault-level singleton encrypted-preferences blob (MYP1 magic) carrying user-controllable preferences. The v0.1 inner schema (MYND-160 + MYND-183 + MYND-110) carries: screen_capture_protection (bool), deliberate_folders (sorted-set string array), auto_lock_seconds (optional integer), editor_layout (optional nested object), the unified manual-sidebar sequences favorites + item_order (item_order is HETEROGENEOUS — note UUIDs + canonical trailing-slash folder paths interleaved, replacing the pre-MYND-183 note_order/folder_order pair), theme (optional 'light'/'dark'/'amoled' string; absence ≡ system / follow-the-OS), and the decoration maps folder_icons (MYND-185 — nested string→string object: canonical folder path → icon name) + item_colors (MYND-184 — nested string→string object: a heterogeneous note-UUID-or-folder-path key → color-slot name). Canonical key order: auto_lock_seconds < deliberate_folders < editor_layout < favorites < folder_icons < item_colors < item_order < screen_capture_protection < theme; within each decoration object the members are emitted in lexicographic KEY order. Optional fields are omitted-when-default, so a screen_capture-only vault stays byte-identical to a pre-MYND-183 blob. The outer envelope is 34-byte fixed-offset (magic + protocol_version + reserved + 24-byte prefs_nonce + 4-byte big-endian ciphertext_len) followed by AEAD-wrapped canonical-JSON plaintext + 32-byte CTX commitment tag (Chan & Rogaway 2022). prefs_key derives from root_key via the canonical DeriveSubkey helper with HKDF context 'myne.v0.1 prefs-key' (no items_key coupling, see grill Q1). AAD binds account_number_hash + the role string 'prefs-blob' (39 bytes total). Read failure surface is non-distinguishing per spec §6.4 + §9.5.5: wrong key, wrong AAD, tampered ciphertext, tampered CTX tag all collapse to a single AeadFailure. Cases generated by `cargo test -p protocol --lib emit_prefs_vectors_for_paste -- --ignored` (in protocol/src/prefs.rs).",
